          "title": {
            "ja": "FMM：直接和・解析配置と展開次数・木の深さ",
            "en": "FMM: direct and analytic references, order and tree depth"
          },
          "method_ids": [
            "fmm"
          ],
          "summary": {
            "ja": "96粒子の2次元対数核を別の全対直接和と照合し、展開次数・木の深さ、回転・平行移動、合力の近似誤差を測ります。",
            "en": "Compare a 96-particle 2D logarithmic kernel with independent all-pairs sums; measure order/depth, rotation/translation and approximate net-force errors."
          },
          "assumptions": {
            "ja": "自由空間のphi=−sum(q log r)、自己項なし。単位正方形は木の包囲領域で、壁・周期境界ではありません。3次元Coulomb核とは別です。",
            "en": "Free-space phi=−sum(q log r), excluding self terms. The unit square bounds the tree and is not a wall or periodic boundary; this is separate from a 3D Coulomb kernel."
          },
          "algorithm": {
            "ja": "P2M/M2M/M2L/L2Lと近接P2Pを保ち、次数2/4/8/12、深さ2/3を比較します。別のCartesian直接和、二点電荷の閉形式、正多角形の中心力と遠方ポテンシャルを参照にします。",
            "en": "Retain P2M/M2M/M2L/L2L and near P2P; compare orders 2/4/8/12 and depths two/three. References include independent Cartesian direct sums, a closed-form charge pair and regular-polygon radial/far-field identities."
          },
          "validation": {
            "ja": "ポテンシャル・場の最大絶対誤差、実際の遠方移動演算、回転・平行移動誤差、電荷を掛けた力の合計を測ります。粗い展開の失敗対照も確認します。",
            "en": "Measure maximum absolute potential/field errors, actual far translations, rotation/translation differences and net charge-weighted force. Detect an inaccurate low-order control."
          },
          "limits": {
            "ja": "木の深さによる相互作用の分割は変わるので、一定次数で深さに対する単調収束は要求しません。対象粒子ごとの展開は厳密な作用反作用を保証せず、3次元・適応木・周期FMM・計算量スケーリングは未検証です。",
            "en": "Interaction repartition changes with depth, so fixed-order depth refinement is not assumed monotone. Target-wise expansions need not preserve exact action/reaction. No 3D, adaptive/periodic FMM or complexity-scaling claim."
          },
          "equations": [
            "\\phi_i=-\\sum_{j\\ne i}q_j\\log|z_i-z_j|,\\qquad\\mathbf F_i=q_i\\mathbf E_i",
            "\\epsilon_E=\\max_i\\|\\mathbf E_i^{\\rm FMM}-\\mathbf E_i^{\\rm direct}\\|_{\\infty}"
